diagnosis_text:
I could not reproduce the outage. Campus 1 subnets (172.16.10.0/24, 172.16.20.0/24, 172.16.30.0/24) are reachable from the rest of the network right now. From an off-campus host (dc_pc5, 10.5.0.5) I successfully pinged 172.16.10.5, 172.16.20.9, and 172.16.30.12 with 0% loss and sub‑3 ms RTTs. From another non-Campus1 host (pc3, 10.6.0.3) I also reached those same Campus 1 hosts, again with 0% loss. These end-to-end tests prove the Campus 1 edge path via router16 and onward to the core is functioning at this time.

Mechanism: If users experienced an earlier loss, it was likely a transient interruption on the Campus 1 edge, which would present as all 172.16.10/20/30 hosts being unreachable from elsewhere while remaining reachable within the building. That symptom matches a brief edge router or uplink issue, but current probing shows it has recovered.

Localization: No active fault found. The tested path traverses the Campus 1 access switches to mswitch0, through router16, and across the router16–router7 interconnect to the broader network; it is operational.

Root cause: Not reproducible; likely a transient flap on the Campus 1 edge (router16 or its uplink) earlier today.

Corrective fix: No action required now. Recommend reviewing router16 interface and system logs for recent flaps and enabling monitoring/alerting on router16 and its uplink to detect and expedite response to any recurrence. === END ===